ed as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Troy Downing (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Troy Downing, a first-term Republican, is seeking re-election in an eastern Montana district that leans 15 points Republican. He won a contested primary in June and has raised about $2.7 million, holding roughly $841,000 on hand. Democrat Brian Miller secured his party's nomination but has raised about $31,000 with little cash remaining, and no outside spending has materialized on either side. An independent and a Libertarian are also on the ballot.\n\nA September poll of registered voters put Downing ahead 48% to 26%, and prediction markets give Republicans roughly a 97% chance of holding the seat. Downing's approval, measured at 34% in May, is modest for an incumbent, but headlines through October describe challengers facing headwinds while he remains in control. The district's partisan lean, the fundraising gap, and the available polling all point to a comfortable Republican win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0084, "margin": -18.82}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0073, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0079, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0127, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.007, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0099, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0089, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0077, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0107, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0119, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0108, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0115, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0131, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0077, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0071, "margin": -20.0}, {"